---

# 24. Acceptance Criteria

### AC-01 — ADK Installation

Google ADK 2 is installed and importable.

### AC-02 — Agent Discovery

The agent is discoverable by:

```bash
adk web
```

### AC-03 — ADK Web

ADK Web starts successfully.

### AC-04 — Agent Selection

`self_improving_agent` appears in ADK Web.

### AC-05 — Docker LLM

The agent communicates with the Docker-hosted Llama 3.2 model.

### AC-06 — Simple Calculation

The agent correctly answers:

```text
Calculate 15% of 200.
```

### AC-07 — Multiple Requests

The agent handles multiple requests during an ADK Web session.

### AC-08 — Natural Language

The agent can answer a general natural-language question.

### AC-09 — Configuration

LLM endpoint and model configuration are externalized.

### AC-10 — Error Handling

An unavailable LLM produces a controlled and understandable error.

### AC-11 — Tests

Automated tests pass:

```bash
uv run pytest
```

### AC-12 — No Memory

No long-term memory is implemented.

### AC-13 — No Self-Improvement

No self-improvement logic is implemented.

### AC-14 — No Custom UI

No custom UI or CLI is implemented.

